{"id": "99aecd153f112fb451ea36273527a655", "text": "stated that the supremacy of the Lord among His hidden forms is of three \ntypes: (i) supreme among similar objects, (ii) supre me among dissimilar \nobjects who share a common condition, and (iii) supreme among objects \nexcept for an obvious leader. For example, among deities, after the Lord, \nthe order of gradation is Sri Lakshmi, Brahma, Vayu, Saraswathi, Bharati, \nSesha, Garuda, Rud ra, Varuni, Sowparni, Parvati and then Indra. However,", "embedding": [-0.025275252759456635, -0.023543350398540497, 0.011969213373959064, -0.03766724467277527, -0.045453205704689026, 0.0028472174890339375, 0.024400295689702034, -0.07468150556087494, -0.003063763491809368, -0.01722160167992115, 0.026340115815401077, -0.026685986667871475, 0.05382339656352997, -0.03919828310608864, 0.07944922149181366, -0.08216337114572525, -0.008880085311830044, -0.014753617346286774, -0.08193186670541763, -0.012679968029260635, 0.08781630545854568, -0.019956648349761963, -0.11168334633111954, -0.007308316882699728, -0.008886062540113926, -0.019767768681049347, 0.03578964248299599, -0.09507933259010315, 0.04067699983716011, -0.07185879349708557, -0.06051061674952507, -0.10074657201766968, -0.00802968256175518, 0.08017629384994507, -0.10164859145879745, 0.038584593683481216, -0.01847674697637558, 0.07590582966804504, 0.06362027674913406, -0.06566542387008667, -0.055536676198244095, -0.019964203238487244, 0.03667690232396126, -0.07743382453918457, 0.06039174646139145, 0.02875874936580658, -0.04207422211766243, 0.00475319242104888, -0.08603717386722565, -0.050798557698726654, -0.024641605094075203, -0.02269233576953411, 0.01146024838089943, 0.11563636362552643, 0.03938395529985428, -0.02799248695373535, -0.0563516840338707, -0.0790969580411911, 0.01182529702782631, -0.017285674810409546, -0.03356897085905075, 0.06634502857923508, -0.006549658253788948, -0.042752522975206375, 0.009593339636921883, -0.0023389148991554976, 0.053217723965644836, -0.0191